<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- One entitlement per TCC service this app touches. These are NOT optional
       decoration: with the hardened runtime on, tccd refuses to even DISPLAY the
       consent prompt for a service whose entitlement is missing. It says so in
       its own log:

         Prompting policy for hardened runtime; service: kTCCServiceAddressBook
         requires entitlement com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook
         but it is missing
         Policy disallows prompt for Sub:{...}

       The failure is silent and looks nothing like a permissions bug. Contacts
       returns denied instantly; Calendar returns false with NO error and leaves
       the status at notDetermined, as though the user had been asked and had
       said nothing. Nobody is ever asked. Running the same binary from a
       terminal HIDES this completely, because a process launched from a shell
       inherits the terminal's own grants and reports success.

       So the list below has to track the code. If a new store is touched in
       src/Permissions.swift and its key is not here, the feature does not
       degrade — it dies without asking, on every machine.

         CNContactStore   -> personal-information.addressbook
         EKEventStore     -> personal-information.calendars
         PHPhotoLibrary   -> personal-information.photos-library
         mic capture      -> device.audio-input

       Not requested, because nothing calls them: camera, location, Apple Events.
       Also no network-client entitlement — the app is not sandboxed and its only
       sockets are loopback. Full Disk Access appears nowhere here on purpose: it
       has no entitlement and no prompt at all, and is granted only in Settings. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.addressbook</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.photos-library</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>

</dict>
</plist>
